  "answer": "### Short Answer\nA corporation must satisfy specific conditions to claim a bad debt as a deductible expense, primarily that the debt must be considered worthless and must have been previously included in gross income.\n\n### Interpretation\n\n### Practical Meaning\nIn practice, this means that corporations should maintain thorough records of their accounts receivable and any efforts made to collect debts. When a debt is deemed uncollectible, the corporation can then deduct it from its taxable income, thereby reducing its overall tax liability. This deduction can be beneficial for managing cash flow and tax obligations, especially in industries where bad debts are common.",
